        <!-- FAQ -->
        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">10. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Who makes Reebok treadmills?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                They are made under licence. The official Reebok Fitness catalogue is operated by RFE International Ltd. of the United Kingdom, which sells the range through regional stores and distributors. Older Reebok treadmills sold in the US in the 2000s were made by ICON Health & Fitness, now iFIT, under an earlier licence. Reebok itself is owned by Authentic Brands Group.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Can you buy a Reebok treadmill in the US?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Not easily. Reebok’s official US equipment store listed no treadmills on 14 October 2026, and Amazon’s US catalogue showed none. Walmart, Academy and Dick’s Sporting Goods have listed models such as the FR30z and Jet 100z, but we could not confirm stock. Buy only a 120-volt unit with a warranty honoured in the US.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the Reebok i-Run treadmill?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                The i-Run is Reebok’s compact folding treadmill for walking and jogging, sold mainly in Britain, Europe and Asia over several generations. The official catalogue lists the i-Run 4.5 and i-Run 5. Figures vary by generation and listing, so check the exact model. We found no i-Run on sale in the US.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What are the specs of the Reebok FR30z?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                A UK retailer, an independent review and a Walmart listing agree on a 4.0 HP peak motor, 12.4 mph top speed and 15 levels of power incline, and the review says it does not fold. User weight conflicts between 264 lb and 330 lb, so confirm it for the unit you buy. It was A$1,698 on Australia’s Reebok store.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Do Reebok treadmills need a subscription?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                No. Current Reebok treadmills work from their own consoles with built-in programmes. Connected models such as the Floatride link over Bluetooth to apps such as Zwift and Kinomap, which are separate paid services you can choose to use. Some listings include a free Kinomap trial, but nothing on the treadmill is locked behind a membership.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Where can I get parts for an old Reebok treadmill?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Start with the model number on the frame sticker. Older US Reebok treadmills were often ICON builds, so iFIT and specialist suppliers that list Reebok (Icon) models are the route. For later models, the Reebok Fitness catalogue site has spare-parts and support pages, with a US support number of 1-800-215-6216.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buying a Reebok Treadmill</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">Most problems with Reebok treadmills come from where they are bought, not the machines. These are the four to avoid.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Importing a 230-volt treadmill</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Most Reebok stock is built for 220 to 240-volt mains. A treadmill’s motor controller is designed for the supply it was sold with, and a converter is a fault and safety risk that voids any warranty. In the US, buy only a unit the seller confirms is built for 120 volts.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Assuming the Reebok name means Reebok support</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Warranty and service come from the licensee’s distributor in your country, or from ICON for older machines. Ask the seller who services the treadmill where you live, for how long on each part, and get it in writing before you order.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Trusting one listing’s figures</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Reebok model names change between markets, and listings for the same machine disagree on capacity, speed and warranty. Check the figure you care about on at least two sources, and treat a single marketplace listing as a claim, not a specification.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Ordering parts for an old Reebok by name</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Older US Reebok treadmills were often ICON builds, and parts suppliers file them separately from later models. Search by the full model number on the frame sticker, not by the name on the console, or you may order a part for a different machine.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

